Source: homelab-dovecot
Section: mail
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-dovecot
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dovecot-core, dovecot-imapd, dovecot-lmtpd, dovecot-pgsql, postgresql-client, adduser
Description: IMAP/LMTP mail delivery wired to the homelab-* shared identity
 Wires Dovecot's SQL passdb to the shared `homelab` Postgres database's
 api.users table via a narrow, column-scoped cross-schema grant (email/
 password_hash/active only -- see script/homelab-dovecot-bootstrap-role),
 so ONE Argon2id password works for both HTTP login (homelab-drive) and
 IMAP/SMTP login -- the unified cross-feature identity design described
 in CLAUDE.md. Also wires an XOAUTH2/OAUTHBEARER oauth2 passdb
 (introspecting against homelab-api's own /api/v1/auth/introspect,
 alongside the SQL passdb, not instead of it) so a homelab-sso-issued
 access token authenticates over real IMAP too -- this is what makes
 Roundcube's SSO login actually reach the mailbox, not just the OAuth
 redirect dance. Static userdb (shared `vmail` system uid/gid, Maildir++
 storage under /var/mail/vhosts/<domain>/<user>) -- this package owns no
 schema/tables of its own and therefore has no migrate role, unlike the
 standard split runtime/migrate Postgres role pattern most other
 homelab-* features use. That's an intentional, documented exception
 (see README.md), not an oversight.
 .
 Exposes LMTP delivery (port 24) and SASL auth (port 12345) both as
 always-on plain-TCP listeners, not local unix sockets -- Postfix
 (homelab-postfix) can be independently placed on a different host,
 pointed here via its own dovecot_host debconf answer. Matches this
 project's own production mail stack, which really runs Postfix and
 Dovecot on separate hosts this way. HAProxy support
 (homelab-dovecot/behind_haproxy, default TRUE -- recommended, matches
 production) adds `haproxy = yes` to the IMAP/IMAPS listeners
 specifically -- never the LMTP/auth ones, which are direct
 Postfix-to-Dovecot data-plane calls that never pass through a proxy.
 Answering false runs this host's IMAP/IMAPS exposed with no proxy in
 front, an explicit opt-out rather than the default.
